  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Agriculture Value Chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency International Cambodia aims to promote transparent and accountable in Cambodia. The overall objective of the project in FAIR4ALL is to promote inclusive and sustainable trade and value chain in banana and rubber sectors in Cambodia that respects human rights, protect environment, and promote women economic empowerment through advocating for fiscal policy that favors more incentives to small scales farmer and compliance enforcement to large scale producers.

The project will provide the evidence and structuredplatform for collective voices and advocacy for reforms and fiscal policy that promotes inclusive and sustainable trade and value chain for smallholders producers and fair competition; and  promote awareness of and capacity to demand for transparent, accountable,progressive fiscal policy that promotes inclusive trade and sustainable value-chain, which favours fair smallholders producers and their communities and enforce strict compliance to international companies in terms of tax andwelfare of workers.

The project will ensure that
1.  Citizens especially smallholder producers will have better understanding of inclusive and sustainable trade and value chain and benefit from tax payment and compliance by companies and traders investing in the sectors.
2. Family rubber planter and banana producer associations will benefit from fair tax compliance and better playing field in the sectors.
3. CSOs have better capacity to influence producers and traders and government to ensure inclusive and sustainable trade and value chain.
4. Workers can benefit from policy that encourages large scale producers to improve their working condition and fiscal compliance.</narrative>
  </description>
