  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency International Cambodia (TI Cambodia) is a fully-accredited National Chapter of Transparency International. Our missionis to work together with individuals and institutions at all levels to promote integrity and reduce corruption in Cambodia.
Transparency International Cambodia (TIC) is a chapter of Transparency International which was established in 2010. Its mission is working to fight corruption, and promote integrity, transparency, and accountability in Cambodia. Oxfam in Cambodia has been in partnership with TIC in 2016 under Finance for Development project.
The initiative named &#x201c;Young Budget Trackers&#x201d; is created to bring together young and potential youth to contribute to policy research and advocacy on open budget, taxation, and pro-poor and FAIR tax and trade policy to the Royal Government of Cambodia to promote fiscal accountability and transparency. The initiative is proposed in line with the current strategic plan of TI Cambodia to engage and empower citizen and youth. It reflects TI Cambodia&#x2019;s goal to strengthen the capacity of citizens and especially youth that serve to bring their interest around a common cause that matters to them such as fiscal accountability and transparency.
Overall Objective:
More open space for citizen and youth to actively engage in fiscal accountability through evident based advocacy on open budget, taxation, pro-poor and FAIR tax and trade policy at national and sub-national levels.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency International Cambodia</narrative>
